[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2961535231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2961535231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2961535231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6whXD_","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T07:23:35Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T07:23:35Z","body":"Note: Seeing we're pretty much in feature freeze for Godot 4.5, this PR is currently set for inclusion in Godot 4.6.\r\n\r\nHowever if consensus is met in time, I'm hoping we can merge this as an experimental feature in Godot 4.5 as the functionality should not impact any users that do not enable it.\r\n\r\nThis is worth further discussion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2961535231/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990469236","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2990469236","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2990469236,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yPvB0","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:28:11Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:29:53Z","body":"@dsnopek @m4gr3d \r\n\r\nOk, I've worked through most of the feedback. Few questions and remarks I've left open up above, so feel free to mark those as resolved if you're happy with the feedback.\r\n\r\nThe biggest structural change is that I've added some XR versions of our binding macros that allow us to bind OpenXR enums and expose them in Godot. I'm pretty happy with this approach and we should slowly clean up existing enums to do the same.\r\nThe only discussion left here is whether we're happy to have the enums live on the objects they most directly related to, or if we should introduce a container class or something. It is possible that the issues here I originally ran into are already solved with improvements I made to the macros later. I'll do some more testing with that tomorrow.\r\n\r\nThe only outstanding task is to complete the logic for the meshes/collision shapes on Mesh2D and Polygon2D entities coming from plane tracking. Should be able to do that over the weekend. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990469236/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990502953","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2990502953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2990502953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yP3Qp","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T09:35:25Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T09:35:25Z","body":"Marked all classes introduced as experimental.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2990502953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991519926","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2991519926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2991519926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yTvi2","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T12:59:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T12:59:26Z","body":"> The biggest structural change is that I've added some XR versions of our binding macros that allow us to bind OpenXR enums and expose them in Godot. I'm pretty happy with this approach and we should slowly clean up existing enums to do the same.\r\n\r\nI think directly exposing OpenXR enums can make sense in the situations were we are effectively directly exposing the OpenXR API, for example, via `OpenXRStructureBase` and its children. Or, even on the extension wrapper classes, when those are meant to be the lower-level interface.\r\n\r\nHowever, for anything that the average developer who just wants to use spatial entity functionality has to interact with, I think this will be confusing. Especially once all the vendor extensions start appearing.\r\n\r\nFor example, right now we've got:\r\n\r\n- `XR_SPATIAL_PLANE_SEMANTIC_LABEL_WALL_EXT`\r\n- `XR_SPATIAL_PLANE_SEMANTIC_LABEL_TABLE_EXT`\r\n\r\n... but this list could get expanded when vendor extensions add (hypothetical) items like:\r\n\r\n- `XR_SPATIAL_PLANE_SEMANTIC_LABEL_SCREEN_META`\r\n- `XR_SPATIAL_PLANE_SEMANTIC_LABEL_WINDOW_BD`\r\n- `XR_SPATIAL_PLANE_SEMANTIC_LABEL_SHELF_ANDROID`\r\n\r\nI think for higher-level stuff, our tendency is to hide these sort of things behind friendlier interfaces. Although, figuring out where to draw the line between low-level and high-level can be tricky too.\r\n\r\nSo, yeah, something we will need to continue to discuss! Probably would be easiest in a call or at an XR team meeting","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991519926/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991623722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2991623722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2991623722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yUI4q","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T13:20:20Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T13:20:20Z","body":"Eventually that will mean adding additional enum values in, potentially through GDExtensions. \r\n\r\nThe reason I'm exposing this level of detail is that those who wish to build those extensions, will need that exposed. It's why I'm exposing even these core objects. Normal users won't ever use them, but those who want to go beyond the base logic will.\r\n\r\nThis is one thing we haven't really got something for, how do we expose something that is not meant for the average user, only for those who are extending the system?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991623722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991683809","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2991683809","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2991683809,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yUXjh","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T13:36:31Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T13:36:31Z","body":"> Normal users won't ever use them, but those who want to go beyond the base logic will.\r\n\r\nI think normal users will want semantic labels, for example, though. And right now this is being exposed as the OpenXR enum directly.\r\n\r\nI think a big part of this discussion will be deciding which bits are low-level and which are high-level. And then how to segregate those two parts clearly.\r\n\r\n> This is one thing we haven't really got something for, how do we expose something that is not meant for the average user, only for those who are extending the system?\r\n\r\nIdeally, I think we'd want to be able to say certain classes are the low-level ones (`OpenXRStructureBase` and children, maybe the extension wrappers?) and then others are the high-level ones (maybe `OpenXRSpatialEntityTracker` and children?)\r\n\r\nFor example, in the godot_openxr_vendors implementation of the Meta spatial entities, the two manager classes (`OpenXRFbSceneManager` and `OpenXRFbSpatialEntityManager`) and the `OpenXRFbSpatialEntity` class are the high-level ones, and all the rest are the low-level ones. Most users can exclusively touch just the high-level ones.\r\n\r\nI personally think we should attempt to do something similar here. And I think the high-level ones shouldn't require directly interacting with enums from OpenXR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991683809/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993515812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2993515812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2993515812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ybW0k","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T10:46:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T10:46:16Z","body":"> I think normal users will want semantic labels, for example, though. And right now this is being exposed as the OpenXR enum directly.\r\n\r\nOwh right, I had forgotten I had also exposed this as is on the `OpenXRPlaneTracker` tracker object, I was thinking of the `OpenXRSpatialComponentPlaneSemanticLabelList` which normal users won't use.\r\n\r\nI think we're kinda stuck here whatever we use our own enum, or that of OpenXR, we don't really have a solid way of adding more enum values to an existing enum. This will always require an update of the thirdparty OpenXR files.\r\n\r\nThis is one of the areas where I'm not sure how vendor extensions will be able to modify core logic and I think that is a bridge we should cross once those extensions are introduced and we can see how they work from an OpenXR POV and if there are changes needed here.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993515812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995224076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-2995224076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":2995224076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yh34M","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T07:16:42Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T07:16:42Z","body":"Rebased, cleaned up a few more things, and implement the missing bits of the `get_mesh` and `get_shape` implementation for `OpenXRPlaneTracker`.\r\n\r\nStill loads of things to further discuss but I think implementation wise everything is complete now.\r\n\r\nOnly real core issue preventing merging as experimental is the discussion David raised, while all the \"low level\" implementations expose things as one would expect, some of this shining through to specifically the implementation of `OpenXRPlaneTracker`, may be something we want to do differently. How however is currently up for debate as we do not yet know how this will evolve in OpenXR land and whether this poses a real problem or not.\r\nThere is an argument that us marking this class as experimental will allow us to tweak the API if we do want to change this part later on.\r\n\r\nThe decision IMHO here will depends on whether this remains the only real issue that needs further discussion, or if other shortcomings are found that make us unsure of the implementation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2995224076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3010963628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-3010963628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":3010963628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zd6is","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-27T01:05:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T01:05:03Z","body":"Decisions in XR Meeting:\r\n1. remove XrStructureType enum, overkill\r\n2. change semantic label on the Tracker to a string, then evaluate if it still makes sense to have the enum in the `OpenXRSpatialComponentPlaneSemanticLabelList` class (or just expose an untyped integer).\r\n3. evaluate the others on a case by case basis. Definite bias to keeping the mirrored approach instead of exposing OpenXR enums directly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3010963628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3055236047","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-3055236047","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":3055236047,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62GzPP","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T03:37:49Z","updated_at":"2025-07-18T02:45:38Z","body":"Ok just pushed a number of changes, I'm not at the end yet and need to clean up a bit of testing code but made the following changes:\r\n1. As discussed `XrStructureType` has been removed as an enum. We're now exposing an int to GDScript/GDExtension\r\n2. The semantic label changes have been done. We now have an enum that mirrors the OpenXR one but is only exposed on the internal `OpenXRSpatialComponentPlaneSemanticLabelList` object. `OpenXRPlaneTracker` now exposes a string.\r\n3. I'm now lazy loading capabilities, we were doing this when the OpenXR instance was created but this was too early, the data is not available until the session was created. As we can't guarantee order of execution between extensions, I'm lazy loading it.\r\n4. There is now a throttle on how often we check plane tracking. Runtimes are supposed to throttle this but we have no guarantee here. We now set a flag when the signal for new plane tracking data is received from the runtime and wait with reacting until 60 frames have passed since the last update. 60 is an arbitrary choice atm and we may wish to make this a setting.\r\n5. We're now checking if the plane tracking data has actually changed with a bit of a margin (> 1 mm) and thus not updating geometry unless needed\r\n\r\nStill todo:\r\n- ~~Fix issue with unpersist anchor not working on some runtimes~~\r\n- Fix issue with `shadow_to_opacity` not working on some runtimes (really issue with the demo)\r\n- ~Expose `XrSpatialPlaneAlignmentEXT` as a mirrored enum~ (and probably check others)\r\n- ~~Test and bugfix markers~~\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3055236047/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068483392","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-3068483392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":3068483392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc625VdA","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T08:51:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T08:51:25Z","body":"Unpersist anchor now works. Fixed several other issues. I think marker tracking should work code wise but it's not detecting things, waiting on feedback from vendors for that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068483392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3076637345","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391#issuecomment-3076637345","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","id":3076637345,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63YcKh","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","